    "narrative": "For LawDog on September 17, **Daulton Varsho** stands out as the clear priority, boasting our highest daily efficiency score at 65.17. His matchup against Lugo is the primary engine here; Lugo\u2019s xERA of 4.59 provides a favorable environment for **Daulton Varsho** to leverage his platoon advantage and elite sprint speed, which remains our highest-weighted priority for SB category climbing. While **Yainer Diaz** (58.67) and **Kyle Karros** (57.59) are both strong starts, **Kyle Karros** is particularly interesting today. Despite a minor penalty for the opponent\u2019s ability to control the run game, **Kyle Karros** benefits from a +14% park factor adjustment, keeping him firmly in the \"Strong\" start tier despite the R/R disadvantage against King.\n\nOur most difficult decision of the morning involved **Zack Gelof**, who ultimately missed the cut with a 38.33 score. The decision to bench **Zack Gelof** was driven by the stifling matchup against Rasmussen (3.30 xERA) and a -17% penalty for the opposing pitcher's skill level. While we value the potential versatility **Zack Gelof** provides, he failed to cross our critical 40.0 floor, leaving him on the bench in favor of higher-floor plays like **Jonathan Aranda** and **Alex Freeland**. We are also keeping a close eye on **Braden Montgomery**; his score of 44.45 is the lowest in the active lineup, largely hampered by the #9 spot in the order. If we see a late-game lineup adjustment that moves **Braden Montgomery** up, his value could pivot sharply, though he currently remains a marginal start.\n\nManagement notes that while our core remains healthy, the proximity of the season end means we are keeping a tight grip on game caps. We have no concerns regarding weather today, but be advised that **Yainer Diaz** and **Gleyber Torres** face mid-rotation arms that are capable of suppressing production if they navigate the middle of the order effectively. We continue to monitor the status of **Jos\u00e9 